# The RAM tiers are symlinks out of the repository. Nothing in them is ever
# committed; they hold logs, screenshots, recorded runs, and scratch that is
# regenerated on demand.
tmp

# Deprecated temporary scripts are kept for exactly one commit and then removed,
# so they are never ignored -- they are supposed to show up in the record once.

# Editor and OS litter.
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# The browsable documentation is a **view**, not a source. Every page under
# docs/HTML is written by ./build-documentation from the Markdown that sits
# beside it. Committing generated pages means every prose edit arrives as a diff
# of itself plus a hundred files of machine output, and it means two people who
# both ran the build have a conflict in something neither of them wrote.
#
# Run ./build-documentation to get them back. Nothing is lost by their absence.
docs/HTML/*
!docs/HTML/.gitkeep

# An exported scene is a **view** of a world, not a source of one. The picture and
# the datafile in scenes/ are both written by ./export-scene out of a map that is
# committed, so committing them means a binary that changes whenever the palette
# does and a diff nobody can read.
#
# A scene traced onto somebody else's picture is different, and lives in
# notes/plans/ where the plan -- which is the source, and is text -- sits beside
# it. See issue 1001.
scenes/*
!scenes/.gitkeep
